{"id":121,"flavor":[{"games":["Shield"],"text":"Starmie swims by spinning its body at high speed. As this Pokémon cruises through the ocean, it absorbs tiny plankton."},{"games":["Sword"],"text":"This Pokémon has an organ known as its core. The organ glows in seven colors when Starmie is unleashing its potent psychic powers."},{"games":["Let’s Go, Eevee!","Let’s Go, Pikachu!"],"text":"The center section is named the core. People think it is communicating when it glows in seven colors."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"It rotates its geometrically shaped body to swim through the water. It always seems to be sending out mysterious radio waves."},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"Its sparkling core is called “the gem of the sea.” This core can be made into high-priced accessories that are traded in secret."},{"games":["Moon"],"text":"Its unusual body shape, reminiscent of abstract art, led local people to spread rumors that this Pokémon may be an invader from outer space."},{"games":["Sun"],"text":"Its shining core is thought to receive and transmit enigmatic signals. It has been known to cause headaches in those who approach it."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Sapphire"],"text":"Starmie swims through water by spinning its star-shaped body as if it were a propeller on a ship. The core at the center of this Pokémon’s body glows in seven colors."},{"games":["Omega Ruby","Ruby"],"text":"Starmie’s center section—the core—glows brightly in seven colors. Because of its luminous nature, this Pokémon has been given the nickname “the gem of the sea.”"},{"games":["Y","White","Black","Platinum","Pearl","Diamond"],"text":"At the center of its body is a red core, which sends mysterious radio signals into the night sky."},{"games":["X","LeafGreen","Blue","Red"],"text":"Its central core glows with the seven colors of the rainbow. Some people value the core as a gem."},{"games":["White 2","Black 2"],"text":"Its core shines in many colors and sends radio signals into space to communicate with something."},{"games":["SoulSilver","Silver"],"text":"Regardless of the environment it lives in, its body grows to form a symmetrical geometric shape."},{"games":["HeartGold"],"text":"The middle section of its body is called the core. It glows in a different color each time it is seen."},{"games":["FireRed"],"text":"This POKéMON has a geometric body. Because of its body, the locals suspect that it is an alien creature."},{"games":["Emerald"],"text":"People in ancient times imagined that STARMIE were transformed from the reflections of stars that twinkled on gentle waves at night."},{"games":["Crystal"],"text":"It is said that it uses the seven- colored core of its body to send electric waves into outer space."},{"games":["Gold"],"text":"The center section of its body is called the core. It glows in a different color each time it is seen."},{"games":["Yellow"],"text":"The center section is named the core. People think it is communicating when it glows in 7 colors."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Illuminate","hidden":false,"description":"By illuminating its surroundings, the Pokémon prevents its accuracy from being lowered."},{"name":"Natural Cure","hidden":false,"description":"The Pokémon's status conditions are cured when it switches out."},{"name":"Analytic","hidden":true,"description":"Boosts the power of the Pokémon's move if it is the last to act that turn."}],"eggGroups":["Water 3"],"genderRate":-1,"hatchCounter":20,"baseHappiness":70,"growthRate":"slow","habitat":"sea","color":"Purple","shape":"Blob","evolution":{"id":120,"name":"Staryu","condition":null,"children":[{"id":121,"name":"Starmie","condition":"Use Water Stone","children":[]}]},"moves":{"game":"Sword / Shield","level":[[1,33],[1,55],[1,56],[1,57],[1,60],[1,94],[1,105],[1,106],[1,107],[1,109],[1,113],[1,129],[1,229],[1,322],[1,362],[1,408]],"machine":[97,502,419,59,362,322,605,291,203,263,430,416,447,360,258,56,63,58,196,113,408,182,94,427,473,240,115,156,496,503,285,214,173,164,57,129,87,86,85,161,271,433,127,250,472],"egg":[],"tutor":[797,812,800]},"cards":[{"id":"me3-118","name":"Mega Starmie ex","set":"Perfect Order","date":"2026-03-27","rarity":"Special Illustration Rare","number":"118","artist":null,"small":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me3-118/small","large":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me3-118/large"},{"id":"me3-21","name":"Mega Starmie ex","set":"Perfect Order","date":"2026-03-27","rarity":"Double Rare","number":"21","artist":null,"small":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me3-21/small","large":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me3-21/large"},{"id":"me3-102","name":"Mega Starmie ex","set":"Perfect Order","date":"2026-03-27","rarity":"Ultra Rare","number":"102","artist":null,"small":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me3-102/small","large":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me3-102/large"},{"id":"sv10-47","name":"Misty's Starmie","set":"Destined Rivals","date":"2025-05-30","rarity":"Uncommon","number":"47","artist":null,"img":"sv10/47"},{"id":"sv4pt5-119","name":"Starmie","set":"Paldean Fates","date":"2024-01-26","rarity":"Shiny Rare","number":"119","artist":"Shigenori Negishi","img":"sv4pt5/119"},{"id":"sv3pt5-121","name":"Starmie","set":"151","date":"2023-09-22","rarity":"Rare","number":"121","artist":"Arai Kiriko","img":"sv3pt5/121"},{"id":"swsh10-30","name":"Starmie V","set":"Astral Radiance","date":"2022-05-27","rarity":"Rare Holo V","number":"30","artist":"Eske Yoshinob","img":"swsh10/30"},{"id":"swsh10-166","name":"Starmie V","set":"Astral Radiance","date":"2022-05-27","rarity":"Rare Ultra","number":"166","artist":"Eske Yoshinob","img":"swsh10/166"},{"id":"swsh10tg-TG13","name":"Starmie V","set":"Astral Radiance Trainer Gallery","date":"2022-05-27","rarity":"Rare Holo V","number":"TG13","artist":"Akira Komayama","img":"swsh10tg/TG13"},{"id":"swsh9-55","name":"Starmie","set":"Brilliant Stars","date":"2022-02-25","rarity":"Uncommon","number":"55","artist":"Akira Komayama","img":"swsh9/55"},{"id":"swsh8-53","name":"Starmie","set":"Fusi